This is how I install my setup from the installer iso,
because when I try to install my full system from the iso it won't work because I will be out of memory.
This way you can do a base install first and then immediately rebuild to your actual setup once booted into the base install.

Remember to setup disko.nix and hardware.nix first!

Install from live iso with:

`sudo nix --extra-experimental-features "nix-command flakes" run "github:nix-community/disko/latest#disko-install" -- --flake .#BaseInstall --disk main /dev/nvme0n1`

(Change /dev/nvme0n1 to your disk!)
 
